    {
      "body": "Tested this change as a backport on v0.27.1 (`vllm/vllm-openai:v0.27.1-cu129-ubuntu2404`, `openai/whisper-large-v3-turbo`) in our serving image — works for us, +1.\n\nWhat we checked:\n\n- **Function level, inside the image.** The unpatched `_get_verbose_segments` raises `IndexError` on `(eos,)` and on `()`; with this patch both return `[]`. On 400 seeded random non-empty token sequences (text tokens, monotonic timestamps, with and without a trailing EOS) plus a single-timestamp answer, the unpatched and the patched function return identical segments, field by field — no behaviour change outside the empty case.\n- **Through the real server code with a stub engine.** `OpenAIServingTranscription.create_transcription` → `_create_speech_to_text` (patched files, only the engine/tokenizer stubbed): a `verbose_json` request where one chunk decodes to EOS only now returns 200 with that chunk contributing no segments, instead of the `IndexError`.\n- **End to end on GPU** (RTX PRO 4000 Blackwell): 33 recordings × `json`/`verbose_json`/`text` × auto/`ru` language — 198 responses byte-identical before and after the patch, all 200.\n\nOne caveat: with large-v3-turbo we could not make the model emit an EOS-only chunk end to end (60+ probes of silence, noise, tones and short trailing chunks — it hallucinates \"Thank you.\" instead), so the crash itself was confirmed at the function level, not from a live request. Our image carries a few other local patches to `speech_to_text`; this hunk applied cleanly on top of them.\n\nAI assistance (Claude) was used to run these checks and to draft this comment.\n",
      "created_at": "2026-10-22T09:09:09Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/58493#issuecomment-6337064527",
      "id": 6337064527,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-22T09:09:09Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "Perlover"
      }
    }
